=== Unsafe-surface gate (every unsafe file is named *_unsafe.rs, so `ls` enumerates it)
./crates/kf-mem/src/sim/tests.rs

★ UNSAFE-SURFACE BREACH — the *_unsafe.rs naming rule.
An auditor must be able to enumerate the ENTIRE unsafe surface with
`ls`: every .rs file that uses the keyword is named *_unsafe.rs, and
the files above are not. Two legitimate fixes, no third:
  - real unsafe code  -> move it into a *_unsafe.rs module, and
    justify the relaxation there (the workspace lint is 'forbid').
  - a comment or doc  -> reword it. Naming the LINT, `unsafe_code`,
    never trips this gate, and neither does the suffix _unsafe.rs.
Never widen the pattern and never add an allowlist: the moment this
gate needs a judgement call, `ls` stops being the audit.
    ★ FAILED

